# rtw89 on the RTOS line, the AP role (A1-A3): the RTL8851BU becomes a
# 2.4 GHz AP (SSID rtos-8851-ap, ch5/2432, HT20, open), the Pi's MT7921AU
# joins it, and the data plane is proven both ways.
#
# The AP MLME is the imported NXP hostapd (CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP); mac80211 keeps
# the AP state machine in the kernel and rtw89 pushes the beacon to the
# firmware over its H2C beacon-update path.  The station's own C5/C6 ladder is
# not this image: the card is beaconing a BSS, not joining one.
#
# What this profile is not: the A4 phase table (rk3568-rtw89-8851bu-ap-tp, a
# separate image on purpose), WPA2, 5 GHz, monitor, and the station role.
#
# The driver + stack are a GPL-2.0 link product; the imported hostapd is
# BSD-3-Clause and the rtw8851b firmware is redistributed with the image
# (docs/LICENSES.md).

CONFIG_BACKEND_FREERTOS=y
CONFIG_OPT_O2=y
CONFIG_PROFILE_BASE=y
CONFIG_HEAP_SIZE=16
CONFIG_CASES="tick rtw89_ap"
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_PCI=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_SDIO=n
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_USB=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_WIRELESS=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_RTW89=y
CONFIG_LIBLINUX80211_NET_LWIP=y
CONFIG_HOSTAP_AP=y
CONFIG_FREERTOS_HEAP_SIZE=16777216
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SIZE=32768
CONFIG_LKPI_USB_CHERRYUSB_STAGE_SLOTS=16
CONFIG_RUNNER_STACK_KB=32
CONFIG_RTW89_USB_BUS=0
